
---

## 📂 Dataset

- 📥 **Source**: [Kaggle - Telco Customer Churn Dataset](https://www.kaggle.com/blastchar/telco-customer-churn)
- 👥 7,043 customer records
- 🎯 Target variable: `Churn` (Yes/No)

---

## 🧹 Data Cleaning & Preprocessing (Python)

- Converted `TotalCharges` from object to float
- Handled missing values using median imputation
- Dropped irrelevant columns like `customerID`
- Encoded categorical variables with `LabelEncoder`
- Applied `SMOTE` to balance the class distribution

---

## 🤖 Modeling

- Model used: **RandomForestClassifier**
- Training with balanced data (`SMOTE`)
- Evaluation on test data:
  - ✅ Accuracy: ~82–84%
  - ✅ ROC-AUC: ~0.84–0.86
- Used `confusion_matrix`, `accuracy_score`, and `roc_auc_score` for evaluation

---

## 📊 Power BI Dashboard Features

- Donut chart showing overall churn rate  
- Stacked bar chart: churn by contract type  
- Histogram: tenure distribution among churners  
- Boxplots: MonthlyCharges and TotalCharges by churn  
- Slicers to filter by services, payment method, and demographics  

> 📁 File: `Telco_Churn_Dashboard.pbix`

---

## 📈 Sample Visuals

![Churn by Contract Type](visuals/churn_by_contract.png)

---

## 💡 Key Insights

- Customers with **month-to-month contracts** churn the most  
- Short tenure customers (less than 6 months) are at **high churn risk**  
- High churn among users **without Online Security or Tech Support**  
- **Paperless billing** linked to higher churn rates

---

## 🛠️ Tools & Technologies

- Python (pandas, seaborn, scikit-learn, imblearn)
- Power BI for dashboarding
- Jupyter Notebook / VS Code

---

## 📌 How to Use

1. Clone this repository  
2. Open and run `churn_model.py` to train the model  
3. Open `Telco_Churn_Dashboard.pbix` in Power BI Desktop  
4. Connect it to `cleaned_churn_data.csv` to refresh visuals

